# Labeled variable states — sugar over chained assignment (CONSTRUCTS row 2)

Catala's `state` steps on one scope variable are pure sugar: the desugarer
collapses each state into its own scopelang variable (`heffing#bruto`,
`heffing#na_aftrek`, …), step n reading step n-1. The plugin lowers each step
as an ordinary internal attribute with its own default tree — no new node, no
state machinery — mangling the `#` to a space (`heffing bruto`, …) so every
downstream read resolves through the ordinary variable table. A step may carry
an exception (its own ladder): here `definitief` doubles the after-deduction
value, or, when `verhoogd`, adds five instead. Own-authored, rights-free.

```catala
declaration scope Trapheffing:
  input grondslag content integer
  input verhoogd content boolean
  output heffing content integer
    state bruto
    state na_aftrek
    state definitief

scope Trapheffing:
  definition heffing state bruto equals grondslag
  definition heffing state na_aftrek equals heffing - 10
  definition heffing state definitief equals heffing * 2
  exception definition heffing state definitief under condition verhoogd consequence equals heffing + 5
```
